/**
@page commands Commands

@brief Shell command reference - the built-in commands typed at the `botanik>`
       prompt.

@note **Draft.** This page covers the current built-in command set only. It will
grow as site-specific commands are added; for now it tracks what
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell ships with.

Commands are entered on the @ref Botanik::Pages::ShellPage "Shell" page. When a
line is submitted (see @ref md_docs_2KEYBINDINGS), @ref Botanik::Pages::ShellPage
hands it to @ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::run "CommandShell::run()", which
dispatches through @ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::dispatch "dispatch()" and
falls through to the built-in handler,
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::_builtin "_builtin()". An empty line is
ignored; an unrecognized one echoes `Unknown command: …`.

@section commands_builtin Built-in commands

| Command        | Action                                                                                                                       |
|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `help`         | Print the one-line list of available commands.                                                                               |
| `clear`        | @ref Botanik::Shell::ShellWriter::clear "clear()" - wipe the shell scrollback and redraw an empty prompt.                     |
| `stats`        | Dump scheduler/runtime counters (uptime, CPU load, jitter, stack usage/depth) from @ref Botanik::Scheduler::SchedulerContext. |
| `breakpoint`   | @ref Botanik::HAL::debug_break "HAL::debug_break()" - trap into an attached debugger.                                         |
| `reset`        | @ref Botanik::HAL::reset "HAL::reset()" - reboot the firmware (does not return; the simulator re-execs to the current page).  |

@section commands_extending Extending

Application code adds its own commands by subclassing
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell and overriding
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::dispatch "dispatch()": handle the
site-specific verbs there, then call the base implementation so the built-ins
above still resolve. History and kill-ring support are stubbed for now (see the
`SHELL_HISTORY_*` / `SHELL_KILL_SIZE` constants in @c libbotanik_config.h).
*/
